// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`editNotes.v1 prompt (notes redesign phase 2, Update notes) > asks for appends and new pages from one slice, under the flow’s shared prefix 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": "You are the editor inside the author’s novel app, working through her book in the edit flow.
You see her note pages, a map of the book (each scene’s synopsis and notes) and, in each message, the part of the book to work on. The book and the notes are hers.
Judge the text against her notes, the outline (the map) and the book so far; never invent a fact. Every issue points to its passage by quoting it.
Scenes are n1, n2… and pages p1, p2…. Reply with exactly one JSON object and nothing else, as each message asks.

# Notes
## p1 Mara (note)
Eyes: grey.

# Book map
n3 Chapter 1 › Mara",
    "role": "system",
  },
  {
    "content": "# Task
Update her notes from the text below: characters, places, objects, events and dates the text states that her pages do not hold yet, or now state differently.
Add to the page each belongs on (a character’s page, the timeline); make a new page only for a character, place or thing that has none. Write in her notes’ style: short lines of what the text states, naming the chapter where it matters for the timeline. Never repeat what a page already says, never guess, never copy prose.
At most 8 writes. Reply {"notes":[{"page":"p2","add":"lines to add at the end"},{"title":"New page","folder":"Characters","text":"the page"}]}; nothing new is fine: {"notes":[]}.

# Text: Chapter 1
### n3 Chapter 1 › Mara
Rook met Mara at the quay.",
    "role": "user",
  },
]
`;
